{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019SEvV5k2qjt893dyosWYt7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/* SPDX-License-Identifier: SunMicrosystems */\n2\t/* Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved. */\n3\t\n4\t/**\n5\t *\n6\t * This file contains a set of functions used by multiple procedures as\n7\t * internal functions. These procedures should not be accessed directly by a\n8\t * user. Note that all procedures are either macros or static inline procedures.\n9\t *\n10\t * Synopsis\n11\t * ========\n12\t *\n13\t * .. code-block:: c\n14\t *\n15\t *     #include \"tools.h\"\n16\t *     EXTRACT_WORDS(ix0,ix1,d);                // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (int, int, double)\n17\t *     GET_HIGH_WORD(i,d);                      // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (int, double)\n18\t *     GET_LOW_WORD(i,d);                       // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (int, double)\n19\t *     INSERT_WORDS(d,ix0,ix1);                 // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (double, int, int)\n20\t *     SET_HIGH_WORD(d,v);                      // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (double, int)\n21\t *     SET_LOW_WORD(d,v);                       // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (double, int)\n22\t *     GET_FLOAT_WORD(i,f);                     // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (int, float)\n23\t *     SET_FLOAT_WORD(f,i);                     // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (float, int)\n24\t *     SAFE_RIGHT_SHIFT(op,amt);                // this macros return value has the same type as input `op`, the inputs are expected to be integer types\n25\t *     double __forced_calculation(double x);\n26\t *     float __forced_calculationf(float x);\n27\t *     double __raise_invalid(void);\n28\t *     float __raise_invalidf(void);\n29\t *     double __raise_div_by_zero(double x);\n30\t *     float __raise_div_by_zerof(float x);\n31\t *     double __raise_overflow(double x);\n32\t *     float __raise_overflowf(float x);\n33\t *     double __raise_underflow(double x);\n34\t *     float __raise_underflowf(float x);\n35\t *     double __raise_inexact(double x);\n36\t *     float __raise_inexactf(float x);\n37\t *     int __issignaling(double x);\n38\t *     int __issignalingf(float x);\n39\t *     REAL_PART(z);                            // this macros return value has the non-complex type of input `z`, the input is expected to be a complex floating-point datum\n40\t *     IMAG_PART(z);                            // this macros return value has the non-complex type of input `z`, the input is expected to be a complex floating-point datum\n41\t *\n42\t * Description\n43\t * ===========\n44\t *\n45\t * ``EXTRACT_WORDS`` is a macro to extract two integer words from a double\n46\t * floating-point datum.\n47\t *\n48\t * ``GET_HIGH_WORD`` is a macro to extract only the highword of the two integer\n49\t * words from a double floating-point datum.\n50\t *\n51\t * ``GET_LOW_WORD`` is a macro to extract only the lowword of the two integer\n52\t * words from a double floating-point datum.\n53\t *\n54\t * ``INSERT_WORDS`` is a macro to insert two integer words into a double\n55\t * floating-point datum.\n56\t *\n57\t * ``SET_HIGH_WORD`` is a macro to insert only the highword of the two integer\n58\t * words into a double floating-point datum.\n59\t *\n60\t * ``SET_LOW_WORD`` is a macro to insert only the lowword of the two integer\n61\t * words into a double floating-point datum.\n62\t *\n63\t * ``GET_FLOAT_WORD`` is a macro to extract the integer representation from a\n64\t * single floating-point datum.\n65\t *\n66\t * ``SET_FLOAT_WORD`` is a macro to insert the integer representation into a\n67\t * single floating-point datum.\n68\t *\n69\t * ``SAFE_RIGHT_SHIFT`` is a macro to avoid undefined behaviour that can arise\n70\t * if the amount of a right shift is exactly equal to the size of the shifted\n71\t * operand. If the amount is equal to the size the macro returns 0.\n72\t *\n73\t * ``__forced_calculation`` is a function to force the execution of the input\n74\t * to go through the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>`. The input for this function is usually\n75\t * an arithmetic operation and not a single value. At the moment the function\n76\t * is only used by others within this file and not expected to be called from\n77\t * outside.\n78\t *\n79\t * ``__raise_invalid`` is a function to force the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>` to generate\n80\t * an ``invalid operation`` exception.\n81\t *\n82\t * ``__raise_div_by_zero`` is a function to force the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>` to\n83\t * generate an ``divide by zero`` exception.\n84\t *\n85\t * ``__raise_overflow`` is a function to force the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>` to\n86\t * generate an ``overflow`` exception.\n87\t *\n88\t * ``__raise_underflow`` is a function to force the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>` to\n89\t * generate an ``underflow`` exception. Even though the library usually does\n90\t * not care about this exception for qualification purposes, the library still\n91\t * tries to conform to the standards (mainly POSIX) in regards to where the\n92\t * exception shall be raised intentionally. In those places this function is\n93\t * used.\n94\t *\n95\t * ``__raise_inexact`` is a function to force the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>` to generate\n96\t * an ``inexact`` exception. Even though the library usually does not care\n97\t * about this exception for qualification purposes, the library still tries to\n98\t * conform to the standards (mainly POSIX) in regards to where the exception\n99\t * shall be raised intentionally. In those places this function is used.\n100\t *\n101\t * ``__issignaling`` is a function to check if a value is a signaling NaN.\n102\t *\n103\t * ``REAL_PART`` is a macro to extract only the real part of a complex\n104\t * floating-point datum.\n105\t *\n106\t * ``IMAG_PART`` is a macro to extract only the imaginary part of a complex\n107\t * floating-point datum.\n108\t *\n109\t * Mathematical Function\n110\t * =====================\n111\t *\n112\t * .. math::\n113\t *\n114\t *    EXTRACT\\_WORDS_{ix0}(d) &= \\text{highword of } d  \\\\\n115\t *    EXTRACT\\_WORDS_{ix1}(d) &= \\text{lowword of } d  \\\\\n116\t *    GET\\_HIGH\\_WORD_{i}(d) &= \\text{highword of } d  \\\\\n117\t *    GET\\_LOW\\_WORD_{i}(d) &= \\text{lowword of } d  \\\\\n118\t *    SET\\_HIGH\\_WORD_{\\text{highword of } d}(d, v) &= d \\text{ with highword } v  \\\\\n119\t *    SET\\_LOW\\_WORD_{\\text{lowword of } d}(d, v) &= d \\text{ with lowword } v  \\\\\n120\t *    GET\\_FLOAT\\_WORD_{i}(d) &= \\text{integer representation of } d  \\\\\n121\t *    SET\\_FLOAT\\_WORD_{d}(i) &= \\text{floating-point representation of } i  \\\\\n122\t *    SAFE\\_RIGHT\\_SHIFT(op, amt) &= \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} op \\gg amt, & amt < \\text{size of } op \\\\ 0, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.  \\\\\n123\t *    \\_\\_forced\\_calculation(x) &= x  \\\\\n124\t *    \\_\\_raise\\_invalid() &= NaN  \\\\\n125\t *    \\_\\_raise\\_div\\_by\\_zero(x) &= \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} -Inf, & x \\in \\mathbb{F}^{-} \\\\ +Inf, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.  \\\\\n126\t *    \\_\\_raise\\_overflow(x) &= \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} -Inf, & x \\in \\mathbb{F}^{-} \\\\ +Inf, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.  \\\\\n127\t *    \\_\\_raise\\_underflow(x) &= \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} -0.0, & x \\in \\mathbb{F}^{-} \\\\ +0.0, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.  \\\\\n128\t *    \\_\\_raise\\_inexact(x) &= x  \\\\\n129\t *    \\_\\_issignaling(x) &= \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} 1, & x = sNaN \\\\ 0, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.  \\\\\n130\t *    REAL\\_PART(z) &= \\Re(z)  \\\\\n131\t *    IMAG\\_PART(z) &= \\Im(z)\n132\t *\n133\t * Returns\n134\t * =======\n135\t *\n136\t * ``EXTRACT_WORDS`` has no return value. It places the two extracted integer\n137\t * words into the parameters ``ix0`` and ``ix1``.\n138\t *\n139\t * ``GET_HIGH_WORD`` has no return value. It places the extracted integer word\n140\t * into the parameter ``i``.\n141\t *\n142\t * ``GET_LOW_WORD`` has no return value. It places the extracted integer word\n143\t * into the parameter ``i``.\n144\t *\n145\t * ``INSERT_WORDS`` has no return value. It places the created double\n146\t * floating-point datum into the parameter ``d``.\n147\t *\n148\t * ``SET_HIGH_WORD`` has no return value. It places the created double\n149\t * floating-point datum into the parameter ``d``.\n150\t *\n151\t * ``SET_LOW_WORD`` has no return value. It places the created double\n152\t * floating-point datum into the parameter ``d``.\n153\t *\n154\t * ``GET_FLOAT_WORD`` has no return value. It places the extracted integer word\n155\t * into the parameter ``i``.\n156\t *\n157\t * ``SET_FLOAT_WORD`` has no return value. It places the created single\n158\t * floating-point datum into the parameter ``f``.\n159\t *\n160\t * ``SAFE_RIGHT_SHIFT`` returns the value ``op`` right shifted by ``amt`` if\n161\t * ``amt`` is smaller than the size of ``op``, otherwise it returns zero.\n162\t *\n163\t * ``__forced_calculation`` returns the input value, or rather the result of\n164\t * the arithmetic calculation used as an input.\n165\t *\n166\t * ``__raise_invalid`` returns ``NaN``.\n167\t *\n168\t * ``__raise_div_by_zero`` returns ``-Inf`` for negative inputs and ``+Inf``\n169\t * for positive inputs.\n170\t *\n171\t * ``__raise_overflow`` returns ``-Inf`` for negative inputs and ``+Inf`` for\n172\t * positive inputs.\n173\t *\n174\t * ``__raise_underflow`` returns ``-0.0`` for negative inputs and ``+0.0`` for\n175\t * positive inputs.\n176\t *\n177\t * ``__raise_inexact`` returns the input value.\n178\t *\n179\t * ``__issignaling`` returns ``1`` if the input value is a signaling ``NaN``,\n180\t * else ``0``.\n181\t *\n182\t * ``REAL_PART`` returns the real part of the input as a floating-point datum\n183\t * of the adequate size.\n184\t *\n185\t * ``IMAG_PART`` returns the imaginary part of the input as a floating-point\n186\t * datum of the adequate size.\n187\t *\n188\t * Exceptions\n189\t * ==========\n190\t *\n191\t * The macros do not raise exceptions.\n192\t *\n193\t * The functions raise the exceptions they are named after, it is their sole\n194\t * purpose. Additionally the procedures ``__raise_overflow`` and\n195\t * ``__raise_underflow`` may raise ``inexact``.\n196\t *\n197\t */\n198\t\n199\t#ifndef LIBMCS_TOOLS_H\n200\t#define LIBMCS_TOOLS_H\n201\t\n202\t#include <limits.h>\n203\t#include <stdbool.h>\n204\t#include <stdint.h>\n205\t\n206\t#include <math.h>\n207\t\n208\t#ifdef __LIBMCS_WANT_COMPLEX\n209\t    #include <complex.h>\n210\t#endif /* __LIBMCS_WANT_COMPLEX */\n211\t\n212\t/* A union which permits us to convert between a double and two 32 bit\n213\t   ints.  */\n214\t\n215\t#ifdef __IEEE_BIG_ENDIAN\n216\t\n217\ttypedef union {\n218\t    double value;\n219\t    struct {\n220\t        uint32_t msw;\n221\t        uint32_t lsw;\n222\t    } parts;\n223\t} ieee_double_shape_type;\n224\t\n225\t#endif\n226\t\n227\t#ifdef __IEEE_LITTLE_ENDIAN\n228\t\n229\ttypedef union {\n230\t    double value;\n231\t    struct {\n232\t        uint32_t lsw;\n233\t        uint32_t msw;\n234\t    } parts;\n235\t} ieee_double_shape_type;\n236\t\n237\t#endif\n238\t\n239\t/* Get two 32 bit ints from a double.  */\n240\t\n241\t#define EXTRACT_WORDS(ix0,ix1,d)                        \\\n242\t    do {                                                \\\n243\t        ieee_double_shape_type ew_u;                    \\\n244\t        ew_u.value = (d);                               \\\n245\t        (ix0) = ew_u.parts.msw;                         \\\n246\t        (ix1) = ew_u.parts.lsw;                         \\\n247\t    } while (0 == 1)\n248\t\n249\t/* Get the more significant 32 bit int from a double.  */\n250\t\n251\t#define GET_HIGH_WORD(i,d)                              \\\n252\t    do {                                                \\\n253\t        ieee_double_shape_type gh_u;                    \\\n254\t        gh_u.value = (d);                               \\\n255\t        (i) = gh_u.parts.msw;                           \\\n256\t    } while (0 == 1)\n257\t\n258\t/* Get the less significant 32 bit int from a double.  */\n259\t\n260\t#define GET_LOW_WORD(i,d)                               \\\n261\t    do {                                                \\\n262\t        ieee_double_shape_type gl_u;                    \\\n263\t        gl_u.value = (d);                               \\\n264\t        (i) = gl_u.parts.lsw;                           \\\n265\t    } while (0 == 1)\n266\t\n267\t/* Set a double from two 32 bit ints.  */\n268\t\n269\t#define INSERT_WORDS(d,ix0,ix1)                         \\\n270\t    do {                                                \\\n271\t        ieee_double_shape_type iw_u;                    \\\n272\t        iw_u.parts.msw = (ix0);                         \\\n273\t        iw_u.parts.lsw = (ix1);                         \\\n274\t        (d) = iw_u.value;                               \\\n275\t    } while (0 == 1)\n276\t\n277\t/* Set the more significant 32 bits of a double from an int.  */\n278\t\n279\t#define SET_HIGH_WORD(d,v)                              \\\n280\t    do {                                                \\\n281\t        ieee_double_shape_type sh_u;                    \\\n282\t        sh_u.value = (d);                               \\\n283\t        sh_u.parts.msw = (v);                           \\\n284\t        (d) = sh_u.value;                               \\\n285\t    } while (0 == 1)\n286\t\n287\t/* Set the less significant 32 bits of a double from an int.  */\n288\t\n289\t#define SET_LOW_WORD(d,v)                               \\\n290\t    do {                                                \\\n291\t        ieee_double_shape_type sl_u;                    \\\n292\t        sl_u.value = (d);                               \\\n293\t        sl_u.parts.lsw = (v);                           \\\n294\t        (d) = sl_u.value;                               \\\n295\t    } while (0 == 1)\n296\t\n297\t/* A union which permits us to convert between a float and a 32 bit\n298\t   int.  */\n299\t\n300\ttypedef union {\n301\t    float value;\n302\t    uint32_t word;\n303\t} ieee_float_shape_type;\n304\t\n305\t/* Get a 32 bit int from a float.  */\n306\t\n307\t#define GET_FLOAT_WORD(i,f)                             \\\n308\t    do {                                                \\\n309\t        ieee_float_shape_type gf_u;                     \\\n310\t        gf_u.value = (f);                               \\\n311\t        (i) = gf_u.word;                                \\\n312\t    } while (0 == 1)\n313\t\n314\t/* Set a float from a 32 bit int.  */\n315\t\n316\t#define SET_FLOAT_WORD(f,i)                             \\\n317\t    do {                                                \\\n318\t        ieee_float_shape_type sf_u;                     \\\n319\t        sf_u.word = (i);                                \\\n320\t        (f) = sf_u.value;                               \\\n321\t    } while (0 == 1)\n322\t\n323\t/* Macros to avoid undefined behaviour that can arise if the amount\n324\t   of a shift is exactly equal to the size of the shifted operand.  */\n325\t\n326\t#define SAFE_RIGHT_SHIFT(op,amt)                        \\\n327\t    (((amt) < 8 * sizeof(op)) ? ((op) >> (amt)) : 0)\n328\t\n329\t/* Exception raising and signaling check functions */\n330\t\n331\tstatic inline double __forced_calculation(double x);\n332\tstatic inline float __forced_calculationf(float x);\n333\t\n334\tstatic inline double __raise_invalid(void);\n335\tstatic inline double __raise_div_by_zero(double x);\n336\tstatic inline double __raise_overflow(double x);\n337\tstatic inline double __raise_underflow(double x);\n338\tstatic inline double __raise_inexact(double x);\n339\t\n340\tstatic inline float __raise_invalidf(void);\n341\tstatic inline float __raise_div_by_zerof(float x);\n342\tstatic inline float __raise_overflowf(float x);\n343\tstatic inline float __raise_underflowf(float x);\n344\tstatic inline float __raise_inexactf(float x);\n345\t\n346\tstatic inline int __issignaling(double x);\n347\tstatic inline int __issignalingf(float x);\n348\t\n349\t\n350\tstatic inline double __forced_calculation(double x) {\n351\t    volatile double r = x;\n352\t    return r;\n353\t}\n354\tstatic inline float __forced_calculationf(float x) {\n355\t    volatile float r = x;\n356\t    return r;\n357\t}\n358\t\n359\tstatic inline double __raise_invalid(void) {\n360\t    double r = __forced_calculation(0.0 / 0.0);\n361\t    return r;\n362\t}\n363\tstatic inline double __raise_div_by_zero(double x) {\n364\t    return (signbit(x) != 0) ? __forced_calculation(-1.0 / 0.0) : __forced_calculation(1.0 / 0.0);\n365\t}\n366\tstatic inline double __raise_overflow(double x) {\n367\t    volatile double huge = 1.0e300;\n368\t    return (signbit(x) != 0) ? -__forced_calculation(huge * huge) : __forced_calculation(huge * huge);\n369\t}\n370\tstatic inline double __raise_underflow(double x) {\n371\t    volatile double tiny = 1.0e-300;\n372\t    return (signbit(x) != 0) ? -__forced_calculation(tiny * tiny) : __forced_calculation(tiny * tiny);\n373\t}\n374\tstatic inline double __raise_inexact(double x) {\n375\t    volatile double huge = 1.0e300;\n376\t    return (__forced_calculation(huge - 1.0e-300) != 0.0) ? x : 0.0;\n377\t}\n378\tstatic inline float __raise_invalidf(void) {\n379\t    float r = __forced_calculationf(0.0f / 0.0f);\n380\t    return r;\n381\t}\n382\tstatic inline float __raise_div_by_zerof(float x) {\n383\t    return (signbit(x) != 0) ? __forced_calculationf(-1.0f / 0.0f) : __forced_calculationf(1.0f / 0.0f);\n384\t}\n385\tstatic inline float __raise_overflowf(float x) {\n386\t    volatile float huge = 1.0e30f;\n387\t    return (signbit(x) != 0) ? -__forced_calculationf(huge * huge) : __forced_calculationf(huge * huge);\n388\t}\n389\tstatic inline float __raise_underflowf(float x) {\n390\t    volatile float tiny = 1.0e-30f;\n391\t    return (signbit(x) != 0) ? -__forced_calculationf(tiny * tiny) : __forced_calculationf(tiny * tiny);\n392\t}\n393\tstatic inline float __raise_inexactf(float x) {\n394\t    volatile float huge = 1.0e30f;\n395\t    return (__forced_calculationf(huge - 1.0e-30f) != 0.0f) ? x : 0.0f;\n396\t}\n397\t\n398\tstatic inline int __issignaling(double x) {\n399\t    uint32_t hx;\n400\t    GET_HIGH_WORD(hx, x);\n401\t    if (isnan(x) && (hx & 0x00080000U) == 0) {\n402\t        return 1;\n403\t    }\n404\t    else {\n405\t        return 0;\n406\t    }\n407\t}\n408\tstatic inline int __issignalingf(float x) {\n409\t    uint32_t ix;\n410\t    GET_FLOAT_WORD(ix, x);\n411\t    if (FLT_UWORD_IS_NAN(ix & 0x7fffffffU) && (ix & 0x00400000U) == 0) {\n412\t        return 1;\n413\t    }\n414\t    else {\n415\t        return 0;\n416\t    }\n417\t}\n418\t\n419\t#ifdef __LIBMCS_WANT_COMPLEX\n420\t    /*\n421\t     * Quoting from ISO/IEC 9899:TC2:\n422\t     *\n423\t     * 6.2.5.13 Types\n424\t     * Each complex type has the same representation and alignment requirements as\n425\t     * an array type containing exactly two elements of the corresponding real type;\n426\t     * the first element is equal to the real part, and the second element to the\n427\t     * imaginary part, of the complex number.\n428\t     */\n429\t    typedef union {\n430\t        float complex z;\n431\t        float parts[2];\n432\t    } float_complex;\n433\t\n434\t    typedef union {\n435\t        double complex z;\n436\t        double parts[2];\n437\t    } double_complex;\n438\t\n439\t    typedef union {\n440\t        long double complex z;\n441\t        long double parts[2];\n442\t    } long_double_complex;\n443\t\n444\t    #define REAL_PART(z)    ((z).parts[0])\n445\t    #define IMAG_PART(z)    ((z).parts[1])\n446\t\n447\t#endif /* __LIBMCS_WANT_COMPLEX */\n448\t\n449\t#endif /* !LIBMCS_TOOLS_H */\n450\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e87a64b-891b-45c4-aafa-3baf54564623","uuid":"3e546c8d-c0ea-4276-acdc-dd81dfe691a8","timestamp":"2026-04-08T00:03:54.313Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/common/tools.h","content":"/* SPDX-License-Identifier: SunMicrosystems */\n/* Copyright (C) 1993 by Sun Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved. */\n\n/**\n *\n * This file contains a set of functions used by multiple procedures as\n * internal functions. These procedures should not be accessed directly by a\n * user. Note that all procedures are either macros or static inline procedures.\n *\n * Synopsis\n * ========\n *\n * .. code-block:: c\n *\n *     #include \"tools.h\"\n *     EXTRACT_WORDS(ix0,ix1,d);                // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (int, int, double)\n *     GET_HIGH_WORD(i,d);                      // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (int, double)\n *     GET_LOW_WORD(i,d);                       // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (int, double)\n *     INSERT_WORDS(d,ix0,ix1);                 // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (double, int, int)\n *     SET_HIGH_WORD(d,v);                      // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (double, int)\n *     SET_LOW_WORD(d,v);                       // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (double, int)\n *     GET_FLOAT_WORD(i,f);                     // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (int, float)\n *     SET_FLOAT_WORD(f,i);                     // this macro has no return value, the inputs are expected to be (float, int)\n *     SAFE_RIGHT_SHIFT(op,amt);                // this macros return value has the same type as input `op`, the inputs are expected to be integer types\n *     double __forced_calculation(double x);\n *     float __forced_calculationf(float x);\n *     double __raise_invalid(void);\n *     float __raise_invalidf(void);\n *     double __raise_div_by_zero(double x);\n *     float __raise_div_by_zerof(float x);\n *     double __raise_overflow(double x);\n *     float __raise_overflowf(float x);\n *     double __raise_underflow(double x);\n *     float __raise_underflowf(float x);\n *     double __raise_inexact(double x);\n *     float __raise_inexactf(float x);\n *     int __issignaling(double x);\n *     int __issignalingf(float x);\n *     REAL_PART(z);                            // this macros return value has the non-complex type of input `z`, the input is expected to be a complex floating-point datum\n *     IMAG_PART(z);                            // this macros return value has the non-complex type of input `z`, the input is expected to be a complex floating-point datum\n *\n * Description\n * ===========\n *\n * ``EXTRACT_WORDS`` is a macro to extract two integer words from a double\n * floating-point datum.\n *\n * ``GET_HIGH_WORD`` is a macro to extract only the highword of the two integer\n * words from a double floating-point datum.\n *\n * ``GET_LOW_WORD`` is a macro to extract only the lowword of the two integer\n * words from a double floating-point datum.\n *\n * ``INSERT_WORDS`` is a macro to insert two integer words into a double\n * floating-point datum.\n *\n * ``SET_HIGH_WORD`` is a macro to insert only the highword of the two integer\n * words into a double floating-point datum.\n *\n * ``SET_LOW_WORD`` is a macro to insert only the lowword of the two integer\n * words into a double floating-point datum.\n *\n * ``GET_FLOAT_WORD`` is a macro to extract the integer representation from a\n * single floating-point datum.\n *\n * ``SET_FLOAT_WORD`` is a macro to insert the integer representation into a\n * single floating-point datum.\n *\n * ``SAFE_RIGHT_SHIFT`` is a macro to avoid undefined behaviour that can arise\n * if the amount of a right shift is exactly equal to the size of the shifted\n * operand. If the amount is equal to the size the macro returns 0.\n *\n * ``__forced_calculation`` is a function to force the execution of the input\n * to go through the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>`. The input for this function is usually\n * an arithmetic operation and not a single value. At the moment the function\n * is only used by others within this file and not expected to be called from\n * outside.\n *\n * ``__raise_invalid`` is a function to force the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>` to generate\n * an ``invalid operation`` exception.\n *\n * ``__raise_div_by_zero`` is a function to force the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>` to\n * generate an ``divide by zero`` exception.\n *\n * ``__raise_overflow`` is a function to force the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>` to\n * generate an ``overflow`` exception.\n *\n * ``__raise_underflow`` is a function to force the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>` to\n * generate an ``underflow`` exception. Even though the library usually does\n * not care about this exception for qualification purposes, the library still\n * tries to conform to the standards (mainly POSIX) in regards to where the\n * exception shall be raised intentionally. In those places this function is\n * used.\n *\n * ``__raise_inexact`` is a function to force the :ref:`FPU <ABBR>` to generate\n * an ``inexact`` exception. Even though the library usually does not care\n * about this exception for qualification purposes, the library still tries to\n * conform to the standards (mainly POSIX) in regards to where the exception\n * shall be raised intentionally. In those places this function is used.\n *\n * ``__issignaling`` is a function to check if a value is a signaling NaN.\n *\n * ``REAL_PART`` is a macro to extract only the real part of a complex\n * floating-point datum.\n *\n * ``IMAG_PART`` is a macro to extract only the imaginary part of a complex\n * floating-point datum.\n *\n * Mathematical Function\n * =====================\n *\n * .. math::\n *\n *    EXTRACT\\_WORDS_{ix0}(d) &= \\text{highword of } d  \\\\\n *    EXTRACT\\_WORDS_{ix1}(d) &= \\text{lowword of } d  \\\\\n *    GET\\_HIGH\\_WORD_{i}(d) &= \\text{highword of } d  \\\\\n *    GET\\_LOW\\_WORD_{i}(d) &= \\text{lowword of } d  \\\\\n *    SET\\_HIGH\\_WORD_{\\text{highword of } d}(d, v) &= d \\text{ with highword } v  \\\\\n *    SET\\_LOW\\_WORD_{\\text{lowword of } d}(d, v) &= d \\text{ with lowword } v  \\\\\n *    GET\\_FLOAT\\_WORD_{i}(d) &= \\text{integer representation of } d  \\\\\n *    SET\\_FLOAT\\_WORD_{d}(i) &= \\text{floating-point representation of } i  \\\\\n *    SAFE\\_RIGHT\\_SHIFT(op, amt) &= \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} op \\gg amt, & amt < \\text{size of } op \\\\ 0, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.  \\\\\n *    \\_\\_forced\\_calculation(x) &= x  \\\\\n *    \\_\\_raise\\_invalid() &= NaN  \\\\\n *    \\_\\_raise\\_div\\_by\\_zero(x) &= \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} -Inf, & x \\in \\mathbb{F}^{-} \\\\ +Inf, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.  \\\\\n *    \\_\\_raise\\_overflow(x) &= \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} -Inf, & x \\in \\mathbb{F}^{-} \\\\ +Inf, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.  \\\\\n *    \\_\\_raise\\_underflow(x) &= \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} -0.0, & x \\in \\mathbb{F}^{-} \\\\ +0.0, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.  \\\\\n *    \\_\\_raise\\_inexact(x) &= x  \\\\\n *    \\_\\_issignaling(x) &= \\left\\{\\begin{array}{ll} 1, & x = sNaN \\\\ 0, & otherwise \\end{array}\\right.  \\\\\n *    REAL\\_PART(z) &= \\Re(z)  \\\\\n *    IMAG\\_PART(z) &= \\Im(z)\n *\n * Returns\n * =======\n *\n * ``EXTRACT_WORDS`` has no return value. It places the two extracted integer\n * words into the parameters ``ix0`` and ``ix1``.\n *\n * ``GET_HIGH_WORD`` has no return value. It places the extracted integer word\n * into the parameter ``i``.\n *\n * ``GET_LOW_WORD`` has no return value. It places the extracted integer word\n * into the parameter ``i``.\n *\n * ``INSERT_WORDS`` has no return value. 